==============================================================================
ROUND 16 -- THE AX-KATZ / CHEVALLEY-WARNING TRANSFER ON (ES)
==============================================================================

==============================================================================
[K0] VALIDATION of the Ax-Katz exponent and Warning's 2nd theorem
==============================================================================
Ax-Katz (Katz 1971):  q^mu | |V|,  mu = ceil((N - sum d_j)/max d_j)
Warning-2:            sum d_j < N and V != {}  =>  |V| >= q^{N-sum d}

  144 random systems brute-forced, 144 of them with mu >= 1.
  Ax-Katz violations: 0.   Warning-2 violations: 0.
  => the exponent formula and the Warning bound are implemented
     correctly and are used unchanged in [K2]-[K6].

==============================================================================
[K1] THE ALGEBRAIZATION (A1): ALG-I indicator and ALG-L locator
==============================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K1a] the banked DP == the weight-profile DP == full brute force
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  (n,p) = (8,17),(8,41),(16,17),(4,13); w = 2,3; every r':
  64 cells, all three counters agree.  The round-15 syndrome DP
  is the ground truth used below.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K1b] ALG-L: the locator system E*F = X^n - 1 counts |W_w| EXACTLY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  variables: the r' non-leading coefficients of monic E (deg r')
  and the n-r' non-leading coefficients of monic F (deg n-r');
  equations: the n coefficient identities of E*F = X^n - 1, each
  of degree 2 (bilinear), plus the window forms (degree 1) on E.
  A monic E of degree r' extends to a solution iff E | X^n - 1,
  and then F is unique -- so the point count is the number of
  size-r' subsets of mu_n meeting the window.

  n    p    w   r'   ALG-L count    |W_w| (DP)    
  8    17   2   1    0              0             
  8    17   3   1    0              0             
  8    17   2   2    4              4             
  8    17   3   2    0              0             
  8    17   2   3    0              0             
  8    17   3   3    0              0             
  8    17   2   4    6              6             
  8    17   3   4    2              2             
  8    41   2   1    0              0             
