  4    13   2   2    2              2             
  4    13   3   2    0              0             
  4    13   2   3    0              0             
  4    13   3   3    0              0             
  20 fixtures, 0 mismatches.
  ALG-L IS AN EXACT ALGEBRAIZATION.  (It also re-verifies Newton
  invertibility: the ELEMENTARY-symmetric prefix e_1..e_{w-1} = 0
  and the POWER-SUM prefix agree at every fixture, since p > w.)
  ALG-L has NO weight equation: deg E = r' is built into the
  variable set, so it is exact at every row, with or without p > n.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K1c] ALG-I: exact iff p > n -- the weight-aliasing failure
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ALG-I's weight form sum_i x_i - r' pins wt(x) only MOD p, so its
  F_q-point count is sum over j = r' (mod p) of |W_w^{(j)}|.
  p > n is FORCED when delta = 1 (n | p-1 => p >= n+1): no
  aliasing, verified in 96 cells.
  witness n = 8, p = 7 (delta = ord_8(7) = 2, so p < n), w = 2:
  weight profile of {x in {0,1}^8 : sum x_i zeta^i = 0 in F_49}
    = [1, 0, 4, 0, 6, 0, 4, 0, 1]
  r' = 1: |W_w| = 0 but the ALG-I system has 1 F_q-points.
  CATCH: at the prize rows delta in {2,4} admits p < n = 2^41
  (p ~ 2^40 for delta = 2), so ALG-I is NOT an exact algebraization
  there; ALG-L is.  Row numbers below are reported for BOTH, with
  ALG-L load-bearing.

==============================================================================
[K2] THE AX-KATZ EXPONENT mu, EXACT, AT THE FOUR ROWS OF RECORD
==============================================================================
formula (pre-registered, P0): mu = ceil((N - sum_j d_j)/max_j d_j),
and q^mu | |V|.  Chevalley-Warning bites iff sum_j d_j < N.

ALG-I extension (over F_q):  N = n; degrees = n copies of 2 (the
   0/1 quadrics) + nforms copies of 1 (window) + 1 (weight).
ALG-I base-field (over F_p): same with nforms -> |Z_w|,
   |Z_w| in [w-1, delta(w-1)].
ALG-L extension (over F_q):  N = n; degrees = n copies of 2 +
   nforms copies of 1.
ALG-L prefix (over F_q):  for a PREFIX window the nforms forced-
   zero coefficients are eliminated outright: N = n - nforms and
   NO linear equations -- the best reading available anywhere.

