------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K3b] P2b -- the p-adic UNIT obstruction at the crossing rows
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Every prime factor of C(L, j) is <= L (a prime > L divides no
  factor of L!).  Here L = n/M <= 2^7 = 128, while p >= 2^39 + 1.

  row                      |W^struct|                               max prime log2      
  crossing w=2^34          23582666872052266206656578733667004800   127       124.1491  
  crossing w=2^35          1777090076065542336                      61        60.6242   
  crossing w=2^36          565722720                                31        29.0755   
  crossing w=2^37          11440                                    13        13.4818   
  crossing w=2^38          56                                       7         5.8074    
  crossing w=2^39          4                                        2         2.0000    

  => p does NOT divide the (ES) target, at ANY crossing row, for
     ANY admissible p, with no case split on delta.  Therefore a
     true statement 'p | |W_w|' is LOGICALLY EQUIVALENT to
     '|W_w| != |W^struct|', i.e. to the EXISTENCE of accidents.
     p-divisibility here is an ACCIDENT-EXISTENCE theorem.  It can
     only REFUTE (ES); it can never prove it.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K3c] P2c -- the WARNING obstruction (kills ALL exact encodings)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Warning-2 (validated in [K0]): sum d < N and V != {} =>
  |V| >= q^{N - sum d}.  Hence for ANY polynomial system over F_q
  whose F_q-point count equals |W_w| EXACTLY: if 0 < |W_w| < q
  then N - sum d <= 0, so mu = ceil((N - sum d)/max d) <= 0.

  max over crossing rows of |W^struct| = C(128,63)
    = 23582666872052266206656578733667004800
    log2 = 124.1491   vs   log2 q > 255.900

  => UNDER (ES), NO EXACT ALGEBRAIZATION OF THE CROSSING COUNT --
     not ALG-I, not ALG-L, not any system anyone will ever write
     down -- CAN HAVE A POSITIVE AX-KATZ EXPONENT.  The vacuity is
     not an artefact of our encoding; it is FORCED.

  NAMED ESCAPE HATCH (registered, and closed here): a FIBERED
  encoding with point count c*|W_w|.  Then q^mu | c*|W_w| is
  consistent -- but by [K3b] gcd(|W_w|, p) = 1 under (ES), so
  q^mu | c.  ALL the divisibility sits in the fibre, where it says
  nothing about |W_w|.  The hatch is information-free.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K3d] the same obstruction run against the SHARPEST refinements
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Moreno-Moreno replaces each d_j by its p-weight degree (sum of
  p-adic digit sums of the exponents).  Every degree in play is 1
  or 2 and p >= 2^39 + 1, so every p-adic digit sum equals the
  degree itself: MM gives EXACTLY the same mu.
  Adolphson-Sperber and Wan sharpen the EXPONENT via the Newton
  polyhedron, but their conclusion has the same SHAPE, 'p^mu |
  count'.  By [K3b] the target is a p-adic UNIT, so no sharpening
  of mu can rescue the family.  The whole p-divisibility toolkit
  -- Chevalley-Warning, Ax, Katz, Ax-Katz, Moreno-Moreno,
  Adolphson-Sperber, Wan, McEliece -- is cut in ONE stroke.

