------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[K4b] McEliece at the four rows of record
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  McEliece: p^{ell-1} divides every weight, ell = least number of
  NONZEROS (repetitions allowed) whose product is 1.
  Our defining set is Z_w = the p-closure of {1,...,w-1}.  0 is
  never in it (0*p^j = 0, and 0 is not in {1,...,w-1}), so
  zeta^0 = 1 IS a nonzero of the code, ell = 1, and McEliece gives
  p^0 = 1.
  verified on 6 fixtures; the argument is uniform in (n, p, w) and
  applies verbatim at n = 2^41.  McEliece: VACUOUS AT EVERY ROW,
  and vacuous for every SHIFTED defining set too (any a >= 1 keeps
  0 out of the closure).  The ONE classical p-divisibility theorem
  that IS defining-set-sensitive is sensitive through a quantity
  (ell) pinned at its trivial value on this whole family.

