  prize rows.  The toy kills the ROW-LEVEL divisibility claim, not
  the method; the METHOD is killed by [K3b]/[K3c].

==============================================================================
[K6] THE ONE LIVE SHAPE (P3): divisibility + upper bound => 0
==============================================================================
  If q^mu | |W| with mu >= 1 AND independently |W| < q^mu, then
  |W| = 0.  This is the ONLY shape in which a p-divisibility
  theorem can PROVE a suppression statement, and it is the
  relevant one at the three BAND rows, where [K3a] showed the
  structural family is EMPTY -- i.e. the target IS a vanishing.

  Ingredient 1: mu >= 1.  Ingredient 2: an UNCONDITIONAL upper
  bound U on |W| with U < q^mu.  The only unconditional bound is
  U = C(n, r').  Needed exponent: mu > log2(U)/log2(q).

  row                      log2 C(n,r')       mu needed        mu available      
  crossing w=2^34          2.198636e+12       8591777919       -1108101562367    
  crossing w=2^35          2.197474e+12       8587236895       -1116691496959    
  crossing w=2^36          2.192823e+12       8569061693       -1133871366143    
  crossing w=2^37          2.174173e+12       8496182070       -1168231104511    
  crossing w=2^38          2.098823e+12       8201729458       -1236950581247    
  crossing w=2^39          1.784019e+12       6971549287       -1374389534719    
  band 1/4 d=4294967297    1.790795e+12       6998025040       -1103806595073    
  band 1/4 d=8589934591    1.797506e+12       7024249866       -1108101562367    
  band 1/8 d=4294967297    1.207313e+12       4717910394       -1103806595073    
  band 1/8 d=8589934591    1.219206e+12       4764386456       -1108101562367    
  band 1/16 d=2147483649   7.50073e+11        2931117587       -1101659111425    
  band 1/16 d=4294967295   7.583864e+11       2963604471       -1103806595071    

  (log2 C(n,r') via lgamma; absolute error << 1 bit on a 2.2e12-bit
   quantity, immaterial.)

  BOTH ingredients fail, by enormous margins:
   - ingredient 1 fails by ~2^41 degree-units ([K2b]);
   - ingredient 2 needs mu ~ 8.6e9 while mu available is ~ -1.1e12.

  WORTH BANKING: with ONLY mu >= 1 plus the band's OWN budget
  0.68 n^2 = 2^81.442 as an a priori bound, the route WOULD close,
  because 2^81.442 < q^1 (q > 2^255.900).  So the entire gap is in
  INGREDIENT 1.  The band rows are the only place in the terminal
  where a p-divisibility theorem could ever have been decisive,
  and there it needs only mu >= 1 -- short by 2^41.

